  "data": "synthetic_microbiology_dataset, seed 2026, as received 2026-10-09",
  "notes": "The live set exactly as shipped: profile excess within specimen (alpha 1e-4), phenotype excess (alpha 1e-3), sampling drop (1e-4), empty run (1e-3), rising trend over 22 pairs (1e-3, D-022 exclusion), and new in an inpatient unit for MRSA and VRE (180 days, D-021 as revised by D-034). Tuned on test: D-020 and D-031 chose their alphas on experiments 0002 and 0009, which ran over all three years and picked the setting by delay on E1 to E4, all inside the scoring period; D-021's 180 days were chosen on E2. Level = 1 (the shipped alphas) reads D1, D2, D3, D4, D6, D7 and I1; D5 sweeps the cluster alphas by m in {100, 30, 10, 3, 1, 0.3, 0.1, 0.03, 0.01}, and its headline is the loosest level with at most 5 cluster and sentinel episodes a year (Choices 3). D2 counts a new-in-unit sentinel as a detection of an injected MRSA clone in an inpatient unit; extra.D2_cluster_signals_only gives the rates over cluster signals alone, which is what experiments 0007 and 0011 counted. D4 is episodes a year over 2024-10-01 to 2026-09-27 with the fixed key and the exclusion zones of Choices 4. I1 counts the detector alerts and new-in-unit alerts; extra.I1_full_tool adds the CPE finds the tool also pushes (D-014). Injected trials run the detectors on the unit and period around the event (the `focus` hint); profile excess is computed for the source's organism and specimen only (0007's rule), which differs from a run on all the data in about 1 of 60 trials (a background signal of another specimen of the same organism in the same unit and weeks). Seed 2026 screening, seeds 2027 to 2030 held out for the _heldout keys; nothing was chosen on either.",
